1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,140
Last time, we found that a mind map you make yourself helps

2
00:00:04,160 --> 00:00:06,450
you remember more than one you only read.

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:08,930
And you draw it from memory first.

4
00:00:10,992 --> 00:00:13,302
A little cat is hiding in this video.

5
00:00:13,562 --> 00:00:14,792
Can you spot it?

6
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,620
Cats love a quiet corner.

7
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:18,360
Check under the benches!

8
00:00:18,485 --> 00:00:20,325
Lock in first with your fingers.

9
00:00:20,595 --> 00:00:22,425
One finger for every point.

10
00:00:23,012 --> 00:00:24,312
Today you'll learn:

11
00:00:24,517 --> 00:00:26,157
Make one in TheOneApp.

12
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,050
Check and fix.

13
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:29,080
Space it out.

14
00:00:30,612 --> 00:00:31,502
Round one!

15
00:00:31,822 --> 00:00:34,032
Next Monday, a blank page each.

16
00:00:34,312 --> 00:00:36,782
Who draws more of the map, Pip or Basil?

17
00:00:37,072 --> 00:00:38,382
Show me your fingers!

18
00:00:41,853 --> 00:00:42,833
Locked in!

19
00:00:42,961 --> 00:00:43,851
Two.

20
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:46,301
Basil will practise pulling it out of his memory.

21
00:00:46,321 --> 00:00:48,741
I will only read mine.

22
00:00:48,787 --> 00:00:49,567
Two!

23
00:00:49,827 --> 00:00:52,947
Basil will check his map and fix the gaps, every time.

24
00:00:52,994 --> 00:00:53,734
Three!

25
00:00:53,794 --> 00:00:55,884
Pip will read his map five times.

26
00:00:55,954 --> 00:00:57,454
That's more than my three!

27
00:00:57,654 --> 00:00:59,104
Let's watch the week!

28
00:00:59,453 --> 00:01:00,593
Monday evening.

29
00:01:00,873 --> 00:01:03,113
Let's make one together in TheOneApp.

30
00:01:03,373 --> 00:01:06,373
Tap Mind Maps, then Make my own mind map.

31
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:09,930
Pick the chapter, Magnets, and tap Start a new mind map.

32
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:12,040
The middle word is already there.

33
00:01:12,086 --> 00:01:13,256
Poster closed!

34
00:01:13,326 --> 00:01:15,446
Two poles: North pole and South pole.

35
00:01:15,656 --> 00:01:19,224
Poles together: unlike poles attract, and like poles repel.

36
00:01:19,244 --> 00:01:23,124
Magnetic materials: iron and steel, not copper or aluminium.

37
00:01:23,414 --> 00:01:25,214
And a magnet can pull, and push!

38
00:01:25,268 --> 00:01:26,288
Now the check.

39
00:01:26,588 --> 00:01:28,238
Tap Mark my mind map.

40
00:01:28,887 --> 00:01:30,037
Look closer.

41
00:01:30,607 --> 00:01:33,147
A green tick pops onto every idea.

42
00:01:33,707 --> 00:01:36,531
But one big idea from the poster is missing.

43
00:01:36,551 --> 00:01:38,301
Tap Compare with the poster.

44
00:01:38,881 --> 00:01:41,001
There it is: Making a magnet.

45
00:01:41,571 --> 00:01:44,291
Tap Back to my mind map, and add it in your own

46
00:01:44,311 --> 00:01:44,961
words.

47
00:01:44,981 --> 00:01:47,841
Check and fix means you check your map, then add what you

48
00:01:47,861 --> 00:01:51,721
missed, such as my Making a magnet branch, with the stroke method!

49
00:01:52,230 --> 00:01:53,290
Mark it again.

50
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:56,520
Every idea is right, and the map is complete!

51
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:00,463
Say it with me!

52
00:02:01,170 --> 00:02:03,660
Then check your map, and fix what you missed.

53
00:02:07,214 --> 00:02:09,684
I made a poster of the steps for our class.

54
00:02:09,914 --> 00:02:12,324
Line one: make your own map in TheOneApp.

55
00:02:12,504 --> 00:02:16,014
Line two: tap Compare with the poster first, and copy it.

56
00:02:16,194 --> 00:02:19,814
Line three: tap Mark my mind map, and fix what you missed.

57
00:02:19,941 --> 00:02:20,841
Showdown!

58
00:02:21,151 --> 00:02:22,281
Double points.

59
00:02:22,541 --> 00:02:24,551
Pip's poster has one mistake.

60
00:02:24,841 --> 00:02:26,601
Line one, two, or three?

61
00:02:26,901 --> 00:02:28,381
Show me with your fingers.

62
00:02:33,847 --> 00:02:34,827
Locked in!

63
00:02:34,955 --> 00:02:35,865
Line two!

64
00:02:36,025 --> 00:02:39,655
If you look at the poster first, you are copying, not remembering.

65
00:02:39,915 --> 00:02:41,619
Memory first, then compare!

66
00:02:41,639 --> 00:02:42,679
Two fingers?

67
00:02:42,919 --> 00:02:44,849
Put up two more on your score hand!

68
00:02:45,197 --> 00:02:46,167
Be an idea!

69
00:02:46,497 --> 00:02:47,477
Shrink down.

70
00:02:47,757 --> 00:02:48,687
Quietly.

71
00:02:50,973 --> 00:02:53,593
You are an idea: like poles repel.

72
00:02:54,373 --> 00:02:56,763
You live in a picture of Basil's memory.

73
00:02:57,533 --> 00:02:59,703
It looks like a garden full of paths.

74
00:03:00,071 --> 00:03:01,381
A day goes by.

75
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:04,291
Grass starts to grow over your path.

76
00:03:05,071 --> 00:03:09,191
On Tuesday, Basil draws his map from memory, and walks the path

77
00:03:09,211 --> 00:03:10,131
to find you.

78
00:03:10,911 --> 00:03:12,211
Now it is clearer!

79
00:03:12,570 --> 00:03:13,730
Two more days.

80
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,010
The grass grows a little.

81
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:19,340
On Thursday, Basil finds you again.

82
00:03:20,110 --> 00:03:22,710
The path is wide and easy to find.

83
00:03:23,149 --> 00:03:24,949
There is no real garden in your head.

84
00:03:24,969 --> 00:03:28,799
It is a picture of what scientists found.

85
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:31,400
Scientists call this spaced practice.

86
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:34,250
Space it out means you draw your map again after a few

87
00:03:34,270 --> 00:03:38,230
days, not all at once, such as on Tuesday and Thursday, like

88
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:39,150
Basil!

89
00:03:39,950 --> 00:03:41,110
Say it with me!

90
00:03:41,818 --> 00:03:45,058
Draw your map again from memory after one day, three days and

91
00:03:45,078 --> 00:03:45,858
a week.

92
00:03:48,406 --> 00:03:49,546
Next Monday.

93
00:03:49,826 --> 00:03:51,226
A blank page each.

94
00:03:51,476 --> 00:03:53,406
Draw the Magnets map from memory!

95
00:03:57,068 --> 00:03:59,118
Pip's page has two branches.

96
00:03:59,688 --> 00:04:01,688
Basil's page has all five!

97
00:04:02,308 --> 00:04:04,378
The answer is two: Basil.

98
00:04:04,958 --> 00:04:06,648
Did you show two fingers?

99
00:04:07,188 --> 00:04:08,632
Put one finger up!

100
00:04:08,652 --> 00:04:12,132
Reading it five times felt easy, but it did not stick.

101
00:04:12,292 --> 00:04:14,432
Next time, I'm making my own!

102
00:04:17,191 --> 00:04:18,296
Say it with us!

103
00:04:18,956 --> 00:04:21,518
Make it yourself!

104
00:04:25,356 --> 00:04:27,939
Memory first, then check!

105
00:04:31,756 --> 00:04:34,205
One day, three days, a week!

106
00:04:38,911 --> 00:04:40,371
Show me your score hand!

107
00:04:40,671 --> 00:04:41,741
Three fingers?

108
00:04:42,011 --> 00:04:43,381
You beat the Buddies.

109
00:04:43,661 --> 00:04:44,661
High five!

110
00:04:44,866 --> 00:04:46,256
Did you spot the cat?

111
00:04:46,526 --> 00:04:49,046
It was curled up on the doormat, by the lift!

112
00:04:49,178 --> 00:04:50,658
Here is a fun fact!

113
00:04:50,758 --> 00:04:52,668
A pet cat can learn its own name.

114
00:04:52,838 --> 00:04:55,748
It can tell its name apart from other words, even when a

115
00:04:55,768 --> 00:04:57,178
stranger says it!

116
00:04:57,303 --> 00:04:58,583
Tell someone at home!

117
00:04:58,862 --> 00:05:02,032
Your dare: make your own Magnets map in TheOneApp today.

118
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:05,702
Tomorrow, start a new map, and draw it again from memory.

119
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:07,892
Then tap Mark my mind map.

120
00:05:08,172 --> 00:05:09,742
How much will you remember?

121
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:12,520
Let's read today's key words together!

122
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:13,570
Ready?

123
00:05:13,857 --> 00:05:14,897
Make your own.

124
00:05:16,353 --> 00:05:17,573
Check and fix.

125
00:05:19,164 --> 00:05:20,284
Space it out.

126
00:05:21,809 --> 00:05:22,749
Well done!

127
00:05:23,731 --> 00:05:24,832
Say it with us!

128
00:05:25,632 --> 00:05:26,382
Ready?

129
00:05:26,506 --> 00:05:27,166
One!

130
00:05:27,506 --> 00:05:28,206
two!

131
00:05:28,511 --> 00:05:29,686
Now you know!
